Z||000000||jlhuber||10-30-1999||05:40 PM||||does anybody know what the "factory" claimed the weight on the 86 gt fastback was?  does anyone know the actual weight of it?  i am curious because i don't know if my little ranger will be able to pull the trailer and the car from michigan to jersey.  the trailer is 2100lbs gross with 6000lbs capacity, so i know the trailer will hold the car.  fyi the car is an '86.5 gt automatic 100% stock...well stock for the moment.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  any help is greatly appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||10-30-1999||07:30 PM||||My 87 GT with automatic and almost all options (sunroof, sub-woofer, spoiler, etc.) and full of gas, weighted 2820 pounds at a certified truck scale.<P>My 308 kit car (built on an 86 GT 5 speed) weighted 2800.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||10-30-1999||07:33 PM||||My 88 coupe with my lard butt, 1/2 tank gas and 62lbs. of extra engine weighs 3104 lbs as per a CAT certified scale at the local truck stop||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||10-31-1999||02:48 AM||||So how does one get their vehicle weighed?  I would imagine pulling into a weigh station would get you laughed at by the truckers and the scale operators.   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||10-31-1999||05:46 AM||||They don't laugh they just sort of smile as they take your $7 and tell you to drive on through the scale. I don't know if the weigh stations on the interstates will weight you but the truck stops will. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||pherder||10-31-1999||08:40 PM||||When I took my 87 GT to get weighed, they took my $7 and gave me my slip.  I told them I would be back with my other car and they said "Whatever"<P>When I showed up with my Ferrari 308 (Fiero rebody), I had EVERYONE out there looking over the car.  Almost got out of there without paying ;^)<P>Paul||||reg||10
